   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the workers' compensation law, in relation to claims for\nattorney's fees; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2021 amending the\nworkers' compensation law relating to attorney's fees, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S. 946-B and A. 1034-B, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7762",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7762-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §24, Work Comp L; amd §2, Chap of 2021 (as proposed in S.946-B & A.1034-B)",
    "lawSection": "Workers' Compensation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7762\n\nSPONSOR: GAUGHRAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the workers' compensation law, in relation to claims for\nattorney's fees; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2021 amending the\nworkers' compensation law relating to attorney's fees, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S. 946-B and A. 1034-B, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2021,\nc.824.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by adding provisions\nregarding written fee applications and amending the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 824 of the Laws of 2021. S.946-B and A.\n1034-B both passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in June 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that section\none of this act shall take effect on the same date and in the same\nmanner as a chapter of the laws of 2021 amending the workers' compen-\nsation law relating to attorney's fees, as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S. 946-B and A. 1034-B, takes effect.\n",
